//! Types moved out of `iyakki_agent::settingstools_net` (F-SPLIT-03, scripted by dist/split/move_types.py); the agent re-exports them.



/// The paragraph for the media server tools, which every person has (the others are for administrators).
pub const MEDIA_RULE: &str = "\nMEDIA SERVER: media_server_status says whether the UPnP/DLNA server is on (free); media_server_set switches it on or off (asks; on lets players on the local network list and play the audio and video of the person's shared folders; off at every sign-out).";

pub const PROMPT_RULE: &str = "\nFIREWALL COUNTS: firewall_counters says how many connections the firewall blocked since its rules were applied and how many each rule of the Firewall page let in (free; administrators). FIREWALL VPN: firewall_vpn_local_status says whether the networks of a connected VPN count as the local network (free); firewall_vpn_local_set switches it (administrators; asks; turning it off must be kept on the Firewall page within 60 s). API SCOPES: devmode_api_scopes lists what each paired computer may call in the web service (free, administrators); devmode_api_scope_set grants or takes back one family such as api:flows or api:flows:read (asks; never api:admin). RELAY: relay_status says whether connections through an owner-run relay are allowed (off by default) and which computers were approved (free, administrators); relay_switch and relay_approve_computer change it (both ask every time; the first contact of a computer also raises a question on the machine's screen that no remote client can answer). CORE CONTRACT: core_contract_status says whether the typed core contract channel of developer mode is on (off by default) and which contract scopes each paired computer holds (free, administrators); core_contract_switch turns the channel on or off and core_contract_scope_set grants or takes back one contract scope of a paired computer (both ask every time; the local-only scope cannot be granted; a remote computer never answers a question or unlocks the vault). UI SOCKET: ui_socket_status says whether the core serves the contract to a UI program on this machine over a unix socket (off by default; no network port) and which scopes it holds (free, administrators); ui_socket_set switches it on or off and sets the contract scopes and the account of that program (asks every time; switching on or granting scopes is a hard ask; the program never unlocks the vault or answers a question).\nONE-CABLE LINK (Settings -> Developer mode -> USB link, administrators, free, nothing is changed): usb_link_check gives the check list of the cable between two computers, each step with what to do when it fails (and the last result in plain words). usb_link_watch is the Replug test: tell the person FIRST to unplug the cable from this computer, wait five seconds and plug it back in, then call it (seconds 5 to 120, default 30; it returns when the other computer appears or the time is over); it says whether this computer's port noticed the cable. Pairing, authorising, the speed test and the link settings are not reachable by chat.\nMAKE ROOM BY SHRINKING (Install to disk; administrators): install_shrink_plan (disk such as sda, part the partition number, to_mib the new size in MiB) shows what would be shrunk, to what size and every step, and changes nothing; always call it first and read it to the person, with the warning to back up. install_shrink asks the person every time (a card with the plan) and then needs `confirm` to be the drive's name exactly as the plan shows it; it checks the file system, shrinks it with the computer's own tool (resize2fs or ntfsresize, which the person installs), checks it again and only then makes the table entry smaller. Only ext2/3/4 and NTFS, never a mounted partition, the running system or the boot stick. Free space made this way is then used by the installer's free-space mode.";
